<group prefix="WebGpuSharp.FFI.">
    <comment location="AdapterHandle">
        <summary>
            Handle to a physical graphics and/or compute device.
            Adapters can be created using Instance::request_adapter or other Instance methods.
            Adapters can be used to open a connection to the corresponding Device on the host system by using Adapter::request_device.
            Does not have to be kept alive.
        </summary>
    </comment>
    <group prefix="AdapterHandle.">
        <comment location="GetFeatures">
            <summary>Get the features supported by the adapter.</summary>
            <param name="features">The features to fill in.</param>
            <returns>the status of the call.</returns>
        </comment>
        <comment location="GetInfo">
            <summary>Get info about the adapter itself.</summary>
            <param name="info">The info to fill in.</param>
            <returns>the status of the call.</returns>
        </comment>
        <comment location="GetLimits">
            <summary>The best limits which can be used to create devices on this adapter.</summary>
            <param name="limits">The limits to fill in.</param>
            <returns>the status of the call.</returns>
        </comment>
        <comment location="HasFeature">
            <summary>Check if and additional functionality is supported by the adapter.</summary>
            <param name="feature">The feature to check.</param>
            <returns>true if the feature is supported.</returns>
        </comment>
        <comment location="RequestDevice">
            <summary>                
                Requests a device from the adapter.
                This is a one-time action: if a device is returned successfully,
                the adapter then enters a "consumed" state
            </summary>
            <param name="options">The device descriptor to use.</param>
            <param name="callbackInfo">The callback to call when the device is ready</param>
        </comment>
    </group>
</group>